+# Add t and use it to check PlaceBlock arguments
+
+## Summary
+
+- Adds the `t` runtime type checker (`osyrisrblx/t`, pinned to `=3.1.1`, the latest release on
+  the Wally index) to `pesde.toml` under the alias `t`. It installs from Wally through pesde like
+  the other packages, into `roblox_packages`, which mounts at `ReplicatedStorage.Packages`.
+- `BlockPlacement.server.luau` now checks the PlaceBlock remote's arguments with one
+  `t.tuple(t.string, isVector3WithoutNaN)` check, which later remotes can follow.
+- Lists `t` in the README's package table.
+
+## Checks kept
+
+Every check the handler made before still runs, in the same order:
+
+| Check | Before | Now |
+|---|---|---|
+| Block type name is a string | `typeof(...) ~= "string"` | `t.string` in the tuple |
+| Position is a Vector3 | `typeof(...) ~= "Vector3"` | `t.Vector3` inside `isVector3WithoutNaN` |
+| Position has no NaN component | `position ~= position` | Same comparison inside `isVector3WithoutNaN`, since `t.Vector3` only checks the type |
+| Block type exists | `BlockTypes.ByName` lookup | Unchanged |
+| Rate limit, character present, cell above ground and free, within reach | Handler code | Unchanged |
+
+The block type lookup stays a lookup instead of `t.keyOf`, because the handler needs the
+`BlockType` it returns anyway. t's checks don't narrow Luau types, so the handler casts
+`blockTypeName :: string` and `position :: Vector3` after the check passes.
+
+## Before testing
+
+1. **Run `pesde install`** at the repo root (stop `rojo serve` first, start it again after). Until
+   then `ReplicatedStorage.Packages.t` doesn't exist and the BlockPlacement script errors at its
+   `require`.
+2. **Commit the updated `pesde.lock`** that the install writes. This PR changes `pesde.toml` but
+   not the lock file, because the install couldn't run while it was written.
+3. Regenerate the sourcemap so luau-lsp can type `t`:
+   `rojo sourcemap default.project.json -o sourcemap.json --include-non-scripts`.
+
+## Not yet verified
+
+The install, `luau-lsp analyze`, `selene`, `stylua --check`, and a playtest have not been run on
+this change. Please run the README's Checks after installing, then playtest:
+
+- Place a block normally: it appears.
+- With the command bar switched to the client during a playtest, call
+  `PlaceBlock:FireServer(...)` with bad arguments: a number as the
+  name, a string as the position, `Vector3.new(0 / 0, 0, 0)`, and an unknown block name. None
+  places a block or errors on the server.
+
+🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)
